  "comments": "There are different variants of the 1977 issue. The stalks of the upper two acorns in the wreath start either at the top of the oak leaves, or they go along the edge of the leaves<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/59e320efdaeab.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/59e320efdaeab.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\nThe 1973 coin (<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/echanges/profil.php?id=150857\">in my collection</a>), although XF/AU looks as if cast and not minted - details are not as sharp or defined. <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5e9030caa1017.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5e9030caa1017.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"199\" height=\"103\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5e9030dc0232b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5e9030dc0232b.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"101\" /></a><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5e90a380aedd3.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5e90a380aedd3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"201\" /></a>",
